e_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.4.1-stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7628) - AMD Ryzen 9 7950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen importing a freshly exported glTF from Blender 4.4.3; the mesh looks correct in the \"Advanced Import\" preview, but after adding mesh to scene (and setting \"Use Vertex Colors as Albedo\", two behaviours can happen:\n- Mesh is all black, no Vertex Colors shown\n- Some colors shown, but obviously corrupted data (like below)\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/85fe33e6-1f81-46c5-b716-f4e7b31d8841)\n\nI originally posted this issue as a [Godot forum post](https://forum.godotengine.org/t/godot-4-4-vertex-colors-import-correctly-but-render-as-black-in-shaders-and-materials/113652), where I got it to work by rebuilding the entire mesh from script.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen MRP, check vertex colors on mesh in scene, double click \"ShaderTest.gltf\" to open it in Advanced Import Preview window; observe.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp_vertex_colors.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20773597/mrp_vertex_colors.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/sta